From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:25:13 +0800
Subject: cli/updater: update from ocelot's GitHub releases

Upstream's updater checks the opencode.ai update service and reinstalls stock
OpenCode. Point it at ocelot instead: the latest version comes from GitHub
releases, and the "curl" install method (a binary in ~/.ocelot/bin) re-runs
ocelot's installer. Package-manager methods are not detected, so an ocelot build
never upgrades a stock OpenCode install found by npm/bun/brew.

`ocelot upgrade` and the background update (config `autoupdate`: true, "notify",
false) then work as they do in OpenCode.

Ocelot-Patch: ocelot/updates

